    pr_ref:  # e623
    description: "Every external boundary Symbol synthesized by\n`ir.create_boundary_nodes` MUST have syntactically valid id slots:\n\n- `language` ∈ the set of known language tokens registered in\n  hypergumbo's analyzer registry.\n- `kind` ∈ the `Symbol.kind` enum (per `docs/schema.json`).\n- `path` is a string that is either `<external>`, `<unknown>`, or a\n  syntactically valid filesystem path (no embedded `:` other than the\n  Dart-style intentional case).\n- `name` is a non-empty string and does not contain `/` or `:` (the\n  id-shape delimiters).\n\nGeneralization of the WI-diruj invariant (Markdown link-target URL\nleaking into `Symbol.language`).\n\n## Currently observed violation (2026-04-25 self-analysis)\n\nTwo orphan boundary nodes:\n\n```\nid=hypergumbo_core/cli.py:<unknown>:0-0:hypergumbo_core/cli.py:hypergumbo_core/cli.py\n  kind=external_symbol  language='hypergumbo_core/cli.py'  path='<external>'\n  in=0  out=0\n```\n\n(Same shape for `hypergumbo_tracker/cli.py`.)\n\nProducer identified: the **TOML analyzer's `[project.scripts]`\nemitter** (`origin='toml-v1'`, `edge_type='defines_target'`,\n`evidence_type='ast_call_direct'`). It emits edges like:\n\n```\nsrc='toml:packages/hypergumbo/pyproject.toml:48-48:hypergumbo:script'\ndst='hypergumbo_core/cli.py'              ← bare path, no language prefix\nmeta={'target_function': 'main'}\n```\n\nThe bare-path `dst` has zero colons, so `_parse_dangling_id` falls\nthrough its `len(parts) < 5` branch (`ir.py:701-706`) and returns\n`(language=path, path='<unknown>', name=path, kind=path)`, which\n`_canonical_external_id` then composes into the leaked id format.\n\n## Two fix surfaces (defense in depth)\n\n**Producer-side (preferred):** TOML analyzer's `[project.scripts]`\nemitter constructs a properly-formed Python module-symbol id for the\nscript target. The script entry `hypergumbo = \"hypergumbo_core.cli:main\"`\nshould resolve to the Python `main` function in\n`packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/cli.py`. If the resolution\nisn't possible cheaply at TOML-analyzer time (Python module → file path\nlookup requires the symbol registry), emit a properly-shaped\n`python:<external>:0-0:hypergumbo_core.cli:main:function` external id\ninstead, which `_parse_dangling_id` will parse correctly into the\nright slots.\n\n**Boundary-side (defensive guard):** `create_boundary_nodes` filters\nout dangling ids whose `language` slot doesn't match a known language\ntoken, OR `_parse_dangling_id`'s `len(parts) < 5` branch returns\nsentinel slots (e.g. `language='unknown'`, `path='<malformed>'`)\ninstead of stuffing the original string into the language slot. Either\nkeeps the leak from reaching the JSON output even if a future producer\nre-introduces the bug.\n\n## Empirical scope sweep\n\nRun `_parse_dangling_id` over every dangling id observed during a full\nself-analysis run and count:\n\n- ids where `len(parts) < 5` (the fallback branch)\n- ids whose `language` slot is not in the known-languages set\n- ids whose `kind` slot is not in the Symbol.kind enum\n\nToday: 2 ids hit the `parts<5` branch (both this TOML-script bug). If\nthat count rises after future analyzer additions, the defensive guard\nis justified.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\nAfter the producer-side fix:\n\n- TOML script-target edges emit a properly-shaped dst id that parses\n  cleanly into the 5 slots.\n- Self-analysis: zero `external_symbol` nodes whose `language` slot\n  contains `/` or ends in `.py`.\n- New invariant test: parametrize over every analyzer, run on a\n  per-language minimal fixture, assert no resulting edge's src/dst is\n  an id with `parts < 5`.\n\n## Validation\n\n1. `pytest` — green, 100% coverage on changed files.\n2. Self-analysis dogfood: zero leaked path-shaped language values.\n3. Tag `awaits_bakeoff_validation` if the fix introduces new\n   `defines_target` edges in larger numbers.\n\n## Status\n\n`violated` — until the producer fix lands. After the producer fix\nlands, transition to `pending_validation` and then `satisfied` once\nself-analysis confirms zero violations.\n\n## Relationship to WI-diruj\n\nWI-diruj fixed exactly this shape for the Markdown analyzer's\nlink-target extractor. This INV generalizes the property and surfaces\na sibling violation in a different producer. The two together\nmotivate the boundary-side defensive guard if a third producer ever\nappears."  # e623
    fields:  # e623
      statement: "Every external boundary Symbol synthesized by ir.create_boundary_nodes has language ∈ known language tokens, kind ∈ Symbol.kind enum, name without '/' or ':' delimiters, and path that is either '<external>', '<unknown>', or a syntactically valid filesystem path."  # e623
      root_cause: "TOML analyzer's [project.scripts] emitter (origin='toml-v1') emits defines_target edges with bare-path dst (no language prefix, no colons), which falls through _parse_dangling_id's parts<5 fallback (ir.py:701-706) and stuffs the path into the language slot of the synthesized boundary id. Same shape as the WI-diruj Markdown bug, different producer. Fix surfaces: (a) toml_config.py emits a properly-formed dst id, (b) defensive guard at _parse_dangling_id sentinel-fills bad slots, or (c) producer-side validation at edge construction."  # e623
